# Frontend Dashboard

**Razorpay AI Builder bar:** The UI exists so reviewers *see* the agentic loop. **Agent Trace** is the hire signal — show decisions + reasoning, not just green/red status. Build the dashboard they’d expect from someone who owns full-loop AI products.

## Priority views

1. Hire-me scroll landing — hero → loop → strategies → delay → live console → scale (mobile + desktop)
2. Live Recovery Feed — status color, clickable rows
3. Agent Trace View — full LangGraph node decisions + LLM reasoning (demo-critical)
4. Recovery Funnel (Recharts)
5. Strategy Performance table

## UX for fintech reviewers

- Dark hire-me storytelling first; Product proof in Live Console
- Show money as ₹ with correct formatting from paise
- Every recovery row must deep-link to its agent trace
- Hover/click should teach the system (agent nodes, strategy cards) without a verbal tour
- Loading / empty / error states; never blank tables that look "broken"
- Prefer clarity over decoration; engineers read the console under time pressure

## Code

- React + TypeScript; typed API clients matching backend schemas
- Colocate view components under `components/` (landing sections + RecoveryFeed, AgentTrace, etc.)
- Do not hide reasoning behind icons — show strategy reasoning text in the trace
- Poll live APIs only when the console section is visible (IntersectionObserver)
